        "prompt": "Analyze the use of Hive. How does Hive interact with Hadoop explain\n in detail\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\nHive is a software tool for data analysis and data transformation on top of Hadoop. Hive provides a query language (HiveQL) that is similar to SQL, and can be used to define and execute data queries and data transformations. Hive also provides a set of data storage and data loading utilities that can be used to interact with Hadoop.\n \n\n Hive is integrated with Hadoop and is often used as the primary data analytics tool for Hadoop-based big data analytics systems. Hive is used for data analysis and transformation, and is often used as a base for developing other data analytics tools. Hive can also be used to define and execute MapReduce jobs, as well as to load and unload data from Hadoop.\n<extra_id_1>User\nFormulate how big data analytics helps business people to increase their revenue. Discuss with any one real time application.\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\nBig data analytics can be used to analyze large amounts of business data to identify patterns and trends that can help business people to make more informed decisions. Big data analytics can also be used to visualize and present data to business people in a clear and concise way, which can help them to make better decisions. For example, big data analytics can be used to analyze customer data to identify patterns that can help business people to increase customer retention, or to analyze sales data to identify patterns that can help business people to increase revenue. Big data analytics can also be used to visualize customer data in order to help business people make better decisions. For example, big data analytics can be used to visualize customer data in order to help business people identify trends in customer behavior.\n<extra_id_1>User\nDraw insights out of any one visualization tool.",
